{
  "_comment": "THE WORKFLOW MATRIX. One row per shipped workflow. A row STATES every key indicator in `key_indicators` -- the writer, its ceiling, the visual lanes, the video engine, the voices, the act shape, the device -- even where the value matches the canonical, because those are decisions and because a machine can REQUIRE one: an 8 GB card needs the small writer whatever the canonical picks, so inheriting it would follow the canonical upward into something that will not fit. Every OTHER key is omitted and inherits from the canonical graph, which is what keeps fps, composite size and caption style out of a reader's way. Pinning is safe here because all 25 rows sit in one column of one file; the drift that once left 82 configs on a retired voice engine was invisible because it was spread over 82 files. Edit this file, run `python scripts/build_variants.py --all`, and the variants and the generated docs are rebuilt together. The variants are GENERATED and are never hand-edited.",
